      <div class="land__inner">
        <p class="land__eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Land acknowledgement</p>
        <h2 id="land-title" class="land__lede">
          InFocus Film School is located on the unceded traditional territories of the
          Musqueam, Squamish and Tsleil-Waututh Nations.
        </h2>

        <ul class="nations">
          {nations.map((n) => (
            <li>
              <a href={n.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <span class="nations__name" lang="und">{n.name}</span>
                <span class="nations__en">{n.en} Nation <span class="arw arw--ext" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <p class="land__text">
          We are grateful to learn, create and tell stories on this land, and we recognize the
          enduring relationship its peoples have with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="page">
      <div class="page__inner">
        <div class="layout">
          <aside class="toc">
            <h2 class="toc__title">On this page</h2>
            <nav aria-label="Table of contents">
              <ol>
                {contents.map(([id, label]) => (
                  <li><a href={`#${id}`} data-toc={id}>{label}</a></li>
                ))}
              </ol>
            </nav>
          </aside>

          <article class="body">
            <section id="funding" data-section>
              <h2>Funding Your Education</h2>
              <p>
                InFocus Film School’s dedication to inclusive education includes supporting First
                Nations, Métis and Inuit students in reaching their artistic and career goals in
                the creative industries. We’re here to help you navigate and access support
                programs that lower the barriers to a quality education.
              </p>

              <div class="stat">
                <div class="stat__figure">
                  <span class="stat__up">Up to</span>
                  <strong>100%</strong>
                  <span class="stat__sub">of tuition subsidized</span>
                </div>
                <div class="stat__body">
                  <p>
                    Eligible students accepted into these programs can have their film school
                    tuition subsidized up to 100%, with non-repayable funding.
                  </p>
                  <ul class="stat__programs">
                    {programs.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              <p>
                There are many routes and funding opportunities for Indigenous students to access
                a film education. For further information or guidance,
                <a href="/contact">contact our Admissions team</a>.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section id="band-funding" data-section>
              <h2>Band Funding</h2>
              <p>
                If you are a First Nations band member, your band may offer scholarships,
                bursaries or other funding that partially or even fully covers your tuition. Each
                band has its own application process to access these funds, and may have deadlines
                or timelines for when you can apply.
              </p>

              <ol class="steps">
                <li>
                  <span class="steps__n">01</span>
                  <span>Contact your band’s post-secondary funding administrator for their application requirements and deadlines.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="steps__n">02</span>
                  <span>Gather the documents they ask for. Our admissions advisors can help with any paperwork from InFocus.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="steps__n">03</span>
                  <span>Apply ahead of your program start date, so funding is in place before classes begin.</span>
                </li>
              </ol>
            </section>

            <section id="scholarships" data-section>
              <h2>Scholarships + Other Funding</h2>
              <p>
                If you are Inuit, Métis or non-status, there are options available to you as well.
                Many sources of external funding and financial support exist for all Indigenous
                students, offered by governments and non-profits across Canada.
              </p>

              <a class="feature" href="https://www.sac-isc.gc.ca/eng/1351185180120/1351685455328" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <span class="feature__tag">Start here</span>
                <span class="feature__title">Indigenous Bursaries Search Tool</span>
                <span class="feature__text">
                  Indigenous Services Canada’s database of bursaries and scholarships. Search for
                  the awards that apply to you.
                </span>
                <span class="feature__cta">Open the search tool <span class="arw arw--ext" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
              </a>

              <h3 class="sub">Other resources to explore</h3>
              <ul class="resources">
                {resources.map((r) => (
                  <li>
                    <a href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                      <span>{r.name}</span>
                      <span class="arw arw--ext resources__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </section>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Truth and Reconciliation. Orange is Orange Shirt Day's colour, used
         only here. -->
    <section class="trc" id="reconciliation" data-section aria-labelledby="trc-title">
      <div class="trc__inner">
        <div class="trc__head">
          <p class="trc__eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Every Child Matters</p>
          <h2 id="trc-title" class="trc__title">Truth and Reconciliation</h2>
          <p class="trc__text">
            From 2008 to 2015, the Truth and Reconciliation Commission of Canada documented the
            history and lasting impacts of the residential school system on Indigenous children,
            families and communities. Its final report issued 94 Calls to Action to redress that
            legacy and advance reconciliation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="trc__num" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="trc__94">94</span>
          <span class="trc__label">Calls to<br />Action</span>
        </div>

        <figure class="trc__quote">
          <span class="trc__qlabel">Call to Action 86</span>
          <blockquote>
            <p>
              We call upon Canadian journalism programs and media schools to require education for
              all students on the history of Aboriginal peoples, including the history and legacy
              of residential schools, the United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous
              Peoples, Treaties and Aboriginal rights, Indigenous law, and Aboriginal–Crown
              relations.
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            Truth and Reconciliation Commission of Canada. As storytellers, media schools like ours
            are called on directly.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <ul class="trc__cards">
          <li class="trc__card">
            <span class="trc__date">
              <strong>30</strong>
              <span>September</span>
            </span>
            <h3>National Day for Truth and Reconciliation</h3>
            <p>
              Also known as Orange Shirt Day, it honours residential school Survivors, their
              families and communities, and the children who never came home.
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.orangeshirtday.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Orange Shirt Society <span class="arw arw--ext" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
          </li>
          <li class="trc__card">
            <span class="trc__icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 5h11a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v11H7a3 3 0 0 1-3-3V5Z M18 8h2v11" /></svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Learn the history</h3>
            <p>
              Read the Commission’s reports and follow Canada’s progress on the Calls to Action.
            </p>
            <a href="https://nctr.ca/records/reports/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NCTR reports <span class="arw arw--ext" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
            <a href="https://www.rcaanc-cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1524494530110/1557511412801" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Progress on the Calls to Action <span class="arw arw--ext" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
          </li>
          <li class="trc__card">
            <span class="trc__icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10Z" /></svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Support is available</h3>
            <p>Free, confidential support for Survivors and their families, 24 hours a day.</p>
            <dl>
              <div>
                <dt>National Residential School Crisis Line</dt>
                <dd><a href="tel:+18669254419">1-866-925-4419</a></dd>
              </div>
